Infrastructure Standards
Networking
	•	External services: Connect to  proxy_net 
	•	Internal services (DBs): Create custom network per project
	•	Never: Expose databases to  proxy_net 
Naming Conventions
	•	Images:  service-name:YYYYMMDD  (date tag for versioning)
	•	Containers:  service-name  (no suffix unless multiple instances)
	•	Networks:  {service-name}_internal 
Security Requirements
	1.	No hardcoded secrets: Always use environment variables
    2.	Non-root containers:  USER node  in Dockerfile when possible
	3.	Minimal base images: Alpine or Distroless preferred
	4.	Health checks: Every service must have  /health  endpoint
	5.	Resource limits: Set  mem_limit  in compose files
12-Factor App Compliance
	•	Config via ENV vars
	•	Dependencies explicitly declared
	•	Stateless processes (use external DBs)
	•	Logs to stdout
	•	Disposable processes
